    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Structured specification for a SQL:2011 temporal query.</para>
<para>For AS_OF queries only start_time is used. For FROM_TO / BETWEEN_AND / CONTAINED_IN both start_time and end_time are used. For ALL neither start_time nor end_time is relevant.</para>
<para>include_deleted: when true, rows that have been logically deleted (i.e. their most-recent version carries an explicit &quot;deleted&quot; flag in their data) are included in the result. When false (default) such rows are excluded. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
